{"title":"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a jar, the ratio of the number of dimes to the number of quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. If the total value of these coins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7624dcadc484bda9f22dbd28147054ace34802b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, how many dimes are in the jar?<br />\n(Each dime is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents, each quarter is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6739c8a3ef02d0f557bfbe01c9c92e562ff9a7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> cents.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total value of the coins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6011dfd7c9ad37496a14135fccab007ec09c4e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4 \\times 100 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" /> in cents.\n</p><p>Since the ratio of the number of dimes to the number of quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, we can let the number of dimes be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and the number of quarters be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Each dime is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents and each quarter is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cents, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f680ca3171984ca21e62b6cca1f746dc0da4b3ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x \\times 10 + 2x \\times 25 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5379d1fa297a42a2c5b0b84a42071cb68378d1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30x + 50x = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db7446876b1046118f22cc29b82e258449b845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80x = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b62f015480815fd34b10c4b8ec0fbc897cf045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{400}{80} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The number of dimes is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7d97a268ef531e75d99b8a87b8126cdfc0cb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 5 = \\boxed{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Verifying_Solution\">Verifying Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Verifying Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the ratio of the number of dimes to the number of quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afb3289ab54a1d7d2e4bff5dc45c2965859244b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> quarters if there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dimes.\n</p><p>The total value of the dimes would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486f0a4b7f68528b8e8bd780544cd63ee0f725f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 15 = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> in cents.\n</p><p>The total value of the quarters would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/08445aede81c533147fa5af04fd236fe98f0ceb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 \\times 10 = 250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> in cents.\n</p><p>The total value of the coins would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3c2f06cab98cbcdf83585a4643247bbc6a608d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150 + 250 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> in cents, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/3883a230456ef12e12d87306a95d8962d008e783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{400}{100} = \\$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />. This matches the actual value of all of the coins, so we have verified our answer.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC\" title=\"2014 CSMC\">2014 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060258\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 169/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/20971